  "notes": [
    "This file owns reusable operating-case/search recipes and the two deterministic rare-contact reproduction anchors. Study-specific numerical guards and pass/fail metrics remain in each study.json.",
    "A targeted contact state is a release-scoped reproduction anchor discovered by a broader search; it still counts only after the production classifier, invariant audit, hybrid continuation, and exact successor checks pass in the consuming study.",
    "The library is not a claim that every listed recipe/state is admissible for every future hardware tune.",
    "General v1.1.2 result studies use defaults/results_reference_model.json, which promotes the secondary helix to a bilateral/slotted topology without altering its signed force/torque equations.",
    "Closure-conditioning intentionally ignores deadzone cases because the 2x2 engaged stick-root map does not exist there."
